{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1792500262,"nonce":"h5/7dvIFjaeC6A2vgIuXzRTxSxc=","message":"Landed in f8cce929546fb14d821d2cf7a3e79d340bfcac24 on main.\n\nThe view preloads along the current scroll direction, retains one departing block for reversals, trims after quiet input and constructs one new block per queued frame. Visible blocks take priority over preload blocks. Height corrections run with InlineFlow's measured-layout work, preserving the current anchor and wheel deltas within the same pass. Measurement-only source text skips redundant intrinsic wrapping; InlineFlow still paints the styled wrapped pieces.\n\nMeasured on the existing Ashui 61510d37 pin, macOS arm64, GPU offscreen at 900x700; UI frame times exclude GPU readback. The styled baseline long-paragraph down glide was p95 102.33 ms / worst 143.15 ms; up was p95 96.40 / worst 147.83; the slow tail had a 77.08 ms mount spike. The final hybrid down glide is p95 24.68 / worst 31.04, up 21.94 / 31.50, tail 0.95 / 1.41. AOT down is 21.84 / 29.41, up 20.58 / 28.12, tail 0.78 / 0.84, cold-up 19.93 / 27.91. These are individual runs, not a universal frame-rate guarantee.\n\nThe baseline had three frames with missing visible blocks. Final down/up/tail/cold-up phases have zero missing frames and zero anchor jumps in both themes and AOT, with at most eight of 250 blocks mounted. The cold-up phase exercises measured-height corrections above the viewport; observed anchor error stayed below 0.001 px. The final check also asserts actual gesture travel, so a missing wheel target cannot produce a false pass.\n\nBoth-theme production Markdown snapshots pass: GFM, inline styles/code, math, Mermaid, links, HTML/details, image disposal, bounded blocks, distant anchors and scroll restoration. Inspected dark math and light restored-end snapshots. Native bin/rayde, bin/rayde.hl and bin/RayDE.app rebuilt. Dependency-pin edit in scripts/deps.sh remains untouched and uncommitted.\n\nReproducer: scripts/markdown-scroll-bench.sh [--native], LIGHT=1 for light. Raw logs under bin/markdown-scroll-{before,final,final-light,native}.log and final assertion run bin/markdown-scroll-final-verified.log. Production snapshots: bin/markdown-glide-snapshots.\n\nRemaining first-mount native layout spikes exceed a 60 Hz budget for long paragraphs; tracked separately in 2998f7804cea1f88f711ca75a0c0599f0c59064954eed91302ca47f74d3360c1. This closes the viewport buffering, range churn and deferred anchor-correction work, not that remaining native-layout optimization.","files":null}]}